\name{etr_plot_poincare_return_map}
\alias{etr_plot_poincare_return_map}
\title{Plot empirical one-dimensional Poincare return map scientific source artists}
\usage{
etr_plot_poincare_return_map(crossings, fit = NULL, strict_source_record = FALSE, ...)
}
\arguments{
\item{crossings}{Native one-dimensional Poincare crossing states with at least two crossings.}\item{fit}{Optional native one-dimensional local affine return map.}\item{strict_source_record}{Logical scalar selecting typed native scientific Matplotlib artist geometry.}\item{...}{Legacy base R graphics options.}
}
\value{Native default invisibly returns consecutive states and optional 100-point affine fit. Strict mode records source successive-crossing scatter, identity diagonal and optional dashed affine return map with exact source axes labels and legend.}
\description{Native scientific geometry for the frozen Python 1.2 nonlinear plotting contract. Scientific estimators and the default base R graphics return are unchanged.}
\details{The strict source record does not return a live Python Matplotlib Axes, accept arbitrary Python dataclasses, reproduce Python exception classes, or establish pixel parity. No independent full-contract certification is claimed.}
